        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Under $900, <strong class="text-white">buy used</strong> — it is the only route to a
            full-size machine at that money, and the value gap is wide enough to justify the
            inspection. Above $2,000, <strong class="text-white">buy new</strong>. In between it
            depends on whether assessing a machine appeals to you or tires you.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you buy secondhand, service it in week one:
            <a href="/treadmill-belt-lubrication/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">lubricate</a>,
            set tension, centre the belt and vacuum out the motor compartment. You are inheriting
            someone else's maintenance history, and forty minutes changes how much life is left.
          </p>
        </div>
